WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.809 --> 00:00:05.340
Thor has kicked alien butt as a member of
the Avengers, fought as a gladiator, and hobnobbed

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:09.171
with the Guardians of the Galaxy, but given
his many, many adventures across the nine

00:00:09.171 --> 00:00:12.450
realms, it can be easy to forget all of his
godly exploits.

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:16.860
Well, fear not: This is Thor's entire MCU
story, finally explained.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:21.800
Yes, Carol Danvers was the first person to
sport the "Avenger" moniker, and Steve Rogers

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:25.589
had the name literally in the title of his
first film, but when you stop to think about

00:00:25.589 --> 00:00:29.020
it, the first Avenger in the MCU to ever draw
breath was Thor.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.360
In fact, the competition isn't even a close
one.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:36.120
As the Odinson reveals in Infinity War, he's
1,500 years old by the time the events of

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.780
the modern MCU roll around.

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:41.020
During that time, Thor has functioned as a
prince of Asgard.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:45.140
He's followed the lead and direction of his
father, Odin, and spent copious amounts of

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.920
time roughhousing with his younger adopted
brother, Loki.

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:52.680
Of the original six Avengers, Thor is also
unique as the only member of royalty on the

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.280
team, as well as the only hero to live off-world.

00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:00.780
By the time he enters the current, 21st-century
MCU timeline, Thor has centuries of experience

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:01.440
under his belt.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:05.720
On top of that, he's operating as the heir
apparent and shoo-in for the next king of

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:06.220
Asgard.

00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:10.400
But, of course, things don't always go according
to plan, especially in the MCU.

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:15.780
By 2011, the aging Odin is ready to crown
his eldest son as the king of Asgard, even

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.260
if Thor is still rather narcissistic and headstrong.

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:22.900
However, the coronation is cut short when
Frost Giants suddenly appear on the scene,

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.340
attempting to raid the royal vault.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:29.200
While the raid fails, it prompts Thor to disobey
his father's orders and head to Jotunheim,

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:33.760
the Frost Giants' home, in order to exact
a little retribution for the unwelcome disturbance.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.300
Thor's disregard for his father's wishes ultimately
leads to Odin stripping his son of his power

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:43.009
and banishing him to Midgard, a backwater
area of the Nine Realms of Asgard known to

00:01:43.009 --> 00:01:44.500
its inhabitants simply as "Earth."

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:49.340
"You are unworthy of these realms!

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:52.180
You are unworthy of your title!

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:53.940
You're UNWORTHY…"

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:59.780
However, as a sign of secret hope for his
son, Odin also sends Thor's magic hammer,

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:03.720
Mjolnir, with him, declaring that only one
who is worthy will be able to wield it.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:08.500
On Earth, Thor meets scientists Erik Selvig
and Jane Foster, and eventually strikes up

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:10.440
a romantic relationship with the latter.

00:02:10.860 --> 00:02:15.000
Over time, he comes to grips with his exile
and is slowly humbled, until he proves himself

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.500
worthy of the hammer, as well as his former
position on Asgard.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.260
At that point, he returns home and defeats
his brother, Loki, who's usurped the throne

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.460
in his absence.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:27.980
Loki ultimately falls to his apparent death,
and a contemplative, more mature Thor then

00:02:27.989 --> 00:02:32.950
resumes his position as his father's right-hand
man, accepting that it isn't his time to rule

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:33.440
as king.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:40.540
One short year after Thor returns to Asgard,
he's sent back to Earth by his father, not

00:02:40.540 --> 00:02:41.520
as an exile, though.

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:45.819
This time, he comes with the express purpose
to fetch his brother Loki after it's discovered

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:49.700
the trickster didn't actually die and is planning
an invasion of Midgard.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:54.520
Upon his arrival, Thor quickly bumps into
the un-unified team of Avengers, immediately

00:02:54.530 --> 00:02:58.250
duking it out with Iron Man before Captain
America convinces them that they shouldn't

00:02:58.250 --> 00:02:59.240
be fighting each other.

00:02:59.829 --> 00:03:03.820
From there, Thor joins the slowly assembling
team on S.H.I.E.L.D.'s Helicarrier, where

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:07.500
he participates in the discussion of what
to do with his brother, providing insight

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:08.900
regarding Loki's past.

00:03:09.190 --> 00:03:12.800
The thunder god even helps contain Hulk when
the Green Machine is accidentally turned loose

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:13.620
on the airship.

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:17.800
After Loki wreaks havoc on the carrier and
escapes, Thor heads to the Big Apple, where

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:21.140
he reunites with the Avengers and participates
in the Battle of New York.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:25.810
The Asgardian plays a thunderous role in the
encounter, fighting hordes of Chitauri and

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:27.800
trading blows with his brother yet again.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:31.640
When the dust settles, Thor takes both Loki
and the Tesseract back to Asgard…although

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:35.080
he nabs a quick bite of shawarma before he
hits the road.

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:50.080
After the 2012 events with the Avengers, Thor
returns home and spends a good deal of time

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.580
traveling the Nine Realms and tending to royal
business.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:57.300
As he takes care of his responsibilities,
though, he never stops pining for Jane Foster.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:01.680
But after he asks the all-seeing Heimdall
to check in on her, Thor is surprised to discover

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:04.160
that his far-sighted friend can no longer
see her.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.760
This revelation spurs the prince to return
to Earth in order to inquire about the whereabouts

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.040
and safety of his sweetheart.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:14.520
Upon his arrival, he finds that she's been
possessed by the Aether, that is, the Reality

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.600
Stone in its "angry sludge" form.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:20.300
Concerned, Thor brings Foster back to Asgard
to receive treatment.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:25.199
In the ensuing chaos, the Dark Elves, led
by Malekith, attack Asgard and kill Thor's

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:25.840
mother, Frigga.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:30.520
This new threat posed by the Dark Elves, the
danger of the Aether inside Jane Foster, and

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:33.560
the death of his mother push Thor to disobey
his father again.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:37.960
He hatches a plan which includes sneaking
out of Asgard with Loki in order to hunt down

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:41.330
Malekith before the Dark Elf can literally
destroy the universe.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:45.419
With the future drama surrounding Thanos,
it's easy to lose sight of the fact that universe-saving

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:47.980
shows up on Thor's resume multiple times.

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.250
The pursuit eventually leads back to Greenwich,
England, where Thor defeats Malekith and does,

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:53.340
indeed, save the universe.

00:04:53.800 --> 00:04:58.440
The next significant event that Thor participates
in is the war with Ultron in 2015.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:03.280
He aids in retrieving Loki's scepter in Sokovia,
and he's present when Ultron is created in

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:07.380
Stark Tower, after which he lends his strength
to the fight against the runaway robot.

00:05:07.990 --> 00:05:12.180
In addition to the superhero antics, Thor
also heads off on a side quest in order to

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:16.380
learn more about a disturbing vision that
he'd received involving the Infinity Stones.

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:21.400
He finds Erik Selvig, who takes him to the
Water of Sights, where he learns, among other

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:23.780
things, that a new being will help destroy
Ultron.

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:27.420
This prompts him to bring Vision to life upon
his return to the Avengers.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:32.280
As the story winds its way to the climactic
events in Sokovia, Thor continues to provide

00:05:32.290 --> 00:05:37.160
muscle and firepower for the Avengers' plans,
and ultimately plays a critical role in foiling

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:40.860
Ultron's attempt to exterminate mankind through
a global catastrophe.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:45.259
With the super-android defeated, Thor heads
off to continue his investigation of the Infinity

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:45.940
Stones.

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:52.040
Thor's search for the Infinity Stones proves
to be fruitless, he and Jane Foster "mutually

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:57.169
dump" each other, and by 2017, he's being
haunted by a new series of dreams, this time

00:05:57.169 --> 00:06:00.120
revolving around Ragnarok and the destruction
of his homeworld.

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:04.900
After exposing Odin as his brother Loki in
disguise, the pair travel to Earth in search

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:05.520
of their father.

00:06:06.020 --> 00:06:10.190
Doctor Strange directs them to Norway, where
they arrive in time to have some parting words

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:12.140
with their dad before he passes away.

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:17.050
While initially tragic, the events soon turn
into a catastrophe, as Odin's death releases

00:06:17.050 --> 00:06:20.580
their evil sister, Hela, from thousands of
years of imprisonment.

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:22.980
"That's not possible."

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:27.120
"Darling, you have no idea what's possible."

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:34.300
Hela quickly shows her superior powers, as
she destroys Mjolnir without skipping a beat.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:38.040
She then prepares to force her brothers to
bow to her so she can take her place as the

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.680
rightful ruler of Asgard.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:44.620
At this point, Loki mistakenly summons the
Bifrost, allowing Hela to follow them directly

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:45.440
to Asgard.

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:49.660
While en route, she sends the two brothers
hurtling out of the beam and into space, where

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.680
they're eventually both deposited on the garbage
planet of Sakaar.

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:57.540
On Sakaar, Thor is captured and forced to
fight as a gladiator in the Grandmaster's

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:00.800
arena, and against his "friend from work,"
Hulk, no less.

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:05.380
After their battle, he helps Bruce Banner
regain control over Hulk and then joins with

00:07:05.380 --> 00:07:07.659
Banner, Valkyrie, and Loki in a daring escape.

00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:12.139
He leads the ragtag band, called the Revengers,
back to Asgard where they plan to overthrow

00:07:12.140 --> 00:07:12.640
Hela.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:17.660
Back on Asgard, the Revengers defeat the goddess
of death, but only by unleashing Ragnarok.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:22.620
As Thor's home planet implodes under Surtur's
fiery heel, the god of thunder escapes with

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:25.980
the Revengers and the survivors of Asgard
on a ship that's headed for Earth.

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:30.680
During the short period of time that leads
up to Ragnarok, Thor loses his father, his

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:35.060
home, most of his people, his hammer, and
even his eye while in combat with his sister.

00:07:35.430 --> 00:07:39.180
Nevertheless, he comes out of the ordeal ready
to lead the remnants of his people as their

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:39.680
king.

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:44.039
Unfortunately, the new king doesn't even finish
the trip to Earth before things take an even

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:45.140
darker turn.

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:48.120
"I feel like everything's gonna work out fine."

00:07:55.340 --> 00:07:59.560
Before Thor and the survivors of Asgard get
to Earth, they're intercepted by Thanos and

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:00.060
his forces.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:05.120
The ensuing encounter leaves half of the Asgardians,
including Heimdall and Loki, dead, the ship

00:08:05.120 --> 00:08:09.500
in tattered ruins, and Thor floating through
space with little to no chance of rescue.

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:14.900
However, when all hope seems lost, the Guardians
of the Galaxy, responding to a distress signal,

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:18.500
arrive on the scene and save the king of Asgard
from a chilly death in space.

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:22.900
Once he regains consciousness, Thor and the
Guardians discuss Thanos and his plans with

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:23.880
the Infinity Stones.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:28.379
This leads the Asgardian to commandeer the
ship's space pod and head off towards Nidavellir

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:31.000
in search of a weapon to replace his beloved
Mjolnir.

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.660
Rocket and Groot tag along, and once the trio
gets there, they attempt to convince the dwarf

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:39.460
king and master smith Eitri to help them forge
the powerful new weapon.

00:08:40.100 --> 00:08:44.540
Eitri is able to do so, but only after Thor
reignites the dormant star forge and takes

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:48.520
the full force of its heat in order to keep
it operating, a feat that almost kills him.

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:53.640
Armed with the freshly forged Stormbreaker,
Thor summons the Bifrost and hurtles back

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:56.860
towards Earth, in order to help his allies
and find Thanos.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:02.020
Thor's epic arrival in Wakanda proves timely,
and he successfully helps to subdue the hordes

00:09:02.020 --> 00:09:05.180
of Outriders that threaten to overwhelm the
Wakandan defenses.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:11.360
Thanos arrives in Wakanda in search of the
last Infinity Stone not long after Thor.

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:15.940
And in a last-ditch effort, the king of Asgard
proves stronger than any of the other heroes

00:09:15.940 --> 00:09:18.920
and lands a solid strike on the Mad Titan
with Stormbreaker.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:23.820
However, he aims for the villain's chest,
inadvertently allowing the wounded but not-at-all-defeated

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:27.050
Thanos to snap his fingers and then disappear.

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:31.080
"You should've gone for the head."

00:09:33.860 --> 00:09:34.360
"NOOOO!"

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.240
Thor is devastated by his failure.

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:42.019
However, a month later, the Avengers discover
Thanos living in retirement on another planet,

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:44.230
and the group jumps at the opportunity for
revenge.

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:49.000
They take Thanos into custody, only to quickly
find that the Infinity Stones are destroyed,

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.540
and it's too late to undo the snap.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:55.260
In a rage, Thor takes Thanos' past advice
and decapitates the villain with a single

00:09:55.260 --> 00:09:55.760
swing.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:58.900
"Perhaps I treated you too harshly."

00:10:01.520 --> 00:10:02.560
"What did you do?"

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:05.100
"I went for the head."

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:10.560
Over the following five years, Thor helps
found New Asgard on Earth, but he eventually

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:12.540
leaves the bulk of the administration to Valkyrie.

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:17.040
In the meantime, he withdraws with his friends,
Korg and Miek, and spends his time drinking

00:10:17.040 --> 00:10:21.660
beer, playing Fortnite, and slowly slipping
into an overweight, despondent state of depression.

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:25.420
"The only thing that IS permanent in life
is impermanence."

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:27.600
"Awesome.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:28.480
Eggs?

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:29.340
Breakfast?"

00:10:29.340 --> 00:10:29.840
"No.

00:10:29.920 --> 00:10:30.940
I'd like a bloody Mary."

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:35.860
When Hulk and Rocket arrive at New Asgard
five full years after the snap, they attempt

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:39.710
to recruit Thor into the Avengers' effort
to travel back in time and undo the damage

00:10:39.710 --> 00:10:41.040
that Thanos has caused.

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:45.300
While Thor is initially reluctant, he finally
agrees to join the venture when he's promised

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:46.310
a whole lot of beer.

00:10:46.780 --> 00:10:51.280
From there, the Odinson finds that his task
is to time travel with Rocket back to Asgard

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:55.740
in 2013, to that very day when his mother
dies, in order to retrieve the Aether.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:11:00.300
Once in Asgard, though, Thor panics and attempts
to flee from his responsibilities, leaving

00:11:00.300 --> 00:11:03.340
Rocket to take care of the unpleasant business
all on his own.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:07.300
In the meantime, Thor has a heart to heart
with his mother and finds new hope.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:11.639
Summoning Mjolnir, he joins Rocket, and the
two head back to the present, arriving at

00:11:11.640 --> 00:11:13.980
the Avengers facility in upstate New York.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.320
Once the Infinity Stones are all gathered,
Thor offers to be the one to snap his fingers

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:22.160
while wearing Stark's Infinity Gauntlet since
he's clearly the strongest Avenger.

00:11:22.460 --> 00:11:26.769
However, he eventually defers to Hulk, who
takes on the responsibility due to his affinity

00:11:26.769 --> 00:11:28.080
with gamma radiation.

00:11:28.400 --> 00:11:32.800
After this, Thor, supercharged once again,
plays a heroic part in the final battle to

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:37.540
overthrow Thanos, wielding both Mjolnir and
Stormbreaker until he lends the former to

00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:39.300
the very worthy Captain America.

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:44.311
Eventually, Tony Stark gives his life to snap
Thanos to ashes, and, once again, the Avengers

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:45.220
save the day.

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:46.940
So what's next for Thor?

00:11:47.200 --> 00:11:51.720
The Asgardian finally finds himself free to
forge his own path for the first time in ages.

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:56.060
He surrenders his kingship to the extremely
capable Valkyrie and then hitches a ride with

00:11:56.060 --> 00:12:00.580
the Guardians of the Galaxy, a move that immediately
causes friction between himself and the crew's

00:12:00.580 --> 00:12:01.220
captain, Star-Lord.

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:05.600
We'll just have to wait until the November
2021 release of Thor: Love and Thunder to

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:09.769
find out what the future has in store for
the mighty Odinson, aside from the timely

00:12:09.769 --> 00:12:11.440
return of his ex…Jane Foster.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:14.220
"Sorry to hear that Jane dumped you."

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:16.340
"She didn't dump me, you know.

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:18.100
I dumped her.

00:12:18.100 --> 00:12:19.420
It was a mutual dumping!"

